---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TeamMember from '../components/TeamMember.astro';
---

<Layout title="Team | AI Safety South Africa">
  <main class="team-main">
    <section class="team-hero">
      <h1 class="text-5xl md:text-6xl text-center text-[#203548] mb-6 px-4 text-display">
        Our Team
      </h1>
      <div class="team-list">
        <TeamMember
          name="Leo Hyams"
          role="Co-Founder, Executive Director"
          image="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/682b664e23519b3b6af8a183/6867e6045c15230d2433d363_headshot_lakefront.jpg"
          link="https://www.linkedin.com/in/leo-hyams-63960a163/#"
        >
          I assist in the daily operation and strategic decision-making of the organization, as well
          as running outreach programs, and doing my personal AI Safety research. I am also a lead
          organizer at the Deep Learning IndabaX South Africa, an annual conference that brings
          together AI researchers, practitioners, and enthusiasts in Africa. Through these roles, I
          apply my computer science and psychology background to create impactful collaborations and
          solve technical problems. Other than this, I'm a regular meditator, as well as a big trail
          runner, both activities I enjoy doing with community in Cape Town.
        </TeamMember>
        <TeamMember
          name="Imaan Khadir"
          role="Operations Generalist"
          image="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/682b664e23519b3b6af8a183/68538bbdcdb7f9e00e114a42_Imaan%20Photoshoot-35-2.jpg"
          link="https://www.linkedin.com/in/imaankhadir/"
        >
          Imaan Khadir is a community builder with over five years of experience in impact-driven
          work and social entrepreneurship. She co-leads Effective Altruism South Africa and focuses
          on AI safety by contributing to projects that build local capacity to navigate AI risks
          and opportunities, with a particular interest in AI Governance in Africa. With a
          background in organising events, growing communities, and driving research in the Global
          South, Imaan is passionate about creating spaces for connection, reflection, and
          meaningful action. She has a Masters in Development Policy and Practice at the University
          of Cape Town's Nelson Mandela School of Public Governance, served as an AI Governance
          Teaching Fellow for BlueDot Impact and was a Don Lavoie Fellow at the Mercatus Center.
        </TeamMember>
        <TeamMember
          name="Benjamin Sturgeon"
          role="Co-Founder, Strategic Advisor"
          image="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/682b664e23519b3b6af8a183/682b664e23519b3b6af8a1e9_se-210.jpg"
          link="https://www.benjaminsturgeon.com/"
        >
          An AI safety researcher based in Cape Town South Africa. My work revolves around
          researching ways to reduce catastrophic risks from transformative AI systems. Currently my
          work focuses on understanding conceptions of agency and trying to develop mathematical
          models of agency so that we can better steer AI systems towards behaviours which enhance
          human agency rather than deplete it. I am also excited about evals that aim to address
          this problem.
        </TeamMember>
        <TeamMember
          name="Tegan Green"
          role="Event Curator"
          image="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/682b664e23519b3b6af8a183/6867e90d2f887c65261a464a_tfg_smol.jpeg"
          link="https://www.linkedin.com/in/tegan-green/"
        >
          As a graduate of the Michaelis School of Fine Art, I think deeply about visual
          communication and interactive experiences. In 2025 I Completed a Cooperative AI course
          which stoked my curiosity about the intersection of interaction design and multi-agent
          systems. With prior experience in User Experience Design, Art Direction and Project
          Management, I'm keen to leverage these skills to build the community and brand at AISSA.
          My aim is to design for cooperative outcomes that support human agency within AI safety.
        </TeamMember>
        <TeamMember
          name="Charl Botha"
          role="Systems & Partnerships"
          image="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/682b664e23519b3b6af8a183/6867e90db611a697e6bdbd42_CharlBotha_Headshot.jpeg"
          link="https://www.linkedin.com/in/botha-charl/"
        >
          I am a technical professional transitioning into the field of AI Safety, building on a
          solid foundation in software development and a BSc in Computer Science &amp; Applied
          Statistics from UCT. My interest in AI advancements predates this dedicated pivot,
          involving active participation in AI Safety Cape Town (AISCT) community discussions, paper
          reading groups, and talks. Currently, I am deepening my expertise through rigorous
          self-study by following the ARENA curriculum, and exploring agent evaluations and
          multi-agent simulations as potential project directions. I am keen to apply my growing AI
          Safety knowledge and development experience to contribute to robust and safe AI systems,
          and I welcome discussions and collaborations.
        </TeamMember>
        <TeamMember
          name="Nicolas Anema"
          role="Content Lead"
          image="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/682b664e23519b3b6af8a183/6867e90f3fae2c8edb2c9bc0_nic_photo.jpg"
          link="https://www.linkedin.com/in/nicolas-anema-70a525271/"
        >
          My interest in technology lies in its capability to enhance human flourishing. While I
          began my studies in Data Science, I deliberately pivoted to a "BSc in AI Applications" to
          concentrate on 'why' of AI's impact, not just the technical 'how'. This focus on the
          practical &amp; ethical dimensions of AI was the perfect springboard for my current
          position as Content Lead for AISSA. In this role, I aim to fuel the South Africa's
          conversation on responsible AI use through our newsletter and LinkedIn presence. I am
          passionate about bridging the gap between developers and the public, ensuring that as we
          build more powerful systems, we do so with a clear-eyed view of their human consequences.
        </TeamMember>
        <TeamMember
          name="Clifford Shearing"
          role="Professorial Fellow"
          image="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/682b664e23519b3b6af8a183/685388f698d1d0395cbea1bf_Clifford%20Shearing%20Profile%20Pic.jpeg"
          link="https://www.linkedin.com/in/clifford-shearing-6305bb1b/"
        >
          Clifford is a governance scholar whose work has focused on the regulation of both existing
          and emerging harm landscapes (harmscapes). His current work is focused on the use of
          process regulation through standards to promote AI safety as well as work on the
          management of risks that AI startups face. Clifford holds professorships at the University
          of Cape Town, the University of Toronto, and the Australian National University.
        </TeamMember>
        <TeamMember
          name="Sam Brown"
          role="Research Scientist"
          image="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/682b664e23519b3b6af8a183/68d3c97da73e81e9d374d0b1_SFB_HAAISS.JPG"
          link="https://www.linkedin.com/in/sam-brown-likes-making-things/"
        >
          Sam Brown is the research lead for small teams who work on evaluating LLM agent behaviour,
          sharing at NeurIPS workshops and being invited to develop evals for the UK AISI. His PhD
          in physics included aspects of machine learning and high-performance computing, after which
          he worked in the startup/university world doing software/data/consulting in the energy and
          environmental sectors. He has been working in AI safety since 2022 and has co-authored AI
          Safety work in ICML.
        </TeamMember>
        <TeamMember
          name="Jaco du Toit"
          role="Research Engineer"
          image="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/682b664e23519b3b6af8a183/68d3cb1b5c133f39b27aced3_JacoDuToitPicture.jpeg"
          link="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jaco-du-toit-a04785208/"
        >
          Jaco du Toit is a machine learning engineer and AI safety researcher based in Cape Town.
          After completing his master’s degree and spending a year in industry, he pivoted to focus
          on AI capability evaluations. He has developed several evals for the UK AI Security
          Institute through their bounty program and is currently working on evals aimed at
          autonomous replication and adaptation risks.
        </TeamMember>
        <TeamMember
          name="Jacy Reese Anthis"
          role="Research Advisor"
          image="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/682b664e23519b3b6af8a183/682b664e23519b3b6af8a1e6_WhatsApp%20Image%202024-07-26%20at%206.00.24%20PM.jpeg"
          link="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jacyanthis/"
        >
          Jacy Reese Anthis is a sociologist, statistician, and co-founder of the Sentience
          Institute, a nonprofit research organization focused on the rise of digital minds and how
          humanity can work with highly capable AI systems. He is also a visiting scholar at the
          Institute for Human-Centered AI (HAI) at Stanford University, a PhD candidate at the
          University of Chicago, and an affiliate with the Center for Human-Compatible AI (CHAI) at
          the University of California, Berkeley. Jacy’s work has been published in top academic
          venues, such as CHI, HRI, and NeurIPS, and featured in global media outlets, such as Vox,
          Forbes, and The Guardian. Jacy has presented his work at conferences and seminars in over
          20 countries, and he lives in the San Francisco Bay Area with his wife Kelly and two
          adopted dogs Apollo and Dionysus.
        </TeamMember>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <style>
    .team-main {
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0d4361 0%, #91a3ab 29%, #efecdf 29%, #efecdf 70%, #e8e8ea 70%, #e8e8ea 100%);
    }

    .team-hero {
      margin-top: 74px;
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
      text-align: center;
    }
    .team-list {
      max-width: 1260px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0.8rem 0 2rem;
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
